#Mission Info

$Version: 0.10
$Name:  XSTR("Autotest Chain", -1)
$Author: Claude
$Created: 10/14/26 at 12:00:00
$Modified: 10/14/26 at 13:00:00
$Notes:
Written by hand (not FRED) as a test of chained events. Based on Tom's Autotest.fs2:
the EMP storm scrambles the player's target, so the unflown autotest player scans the
freighter. The scan starts a chain of events, each one a few seconds after the last,
and the last one starts the supernova. Run with a longer time limit: -at_time 300.
autotest: mission controls vulnerability
The player starts invulnerable and is made vulnerable just before the supernova, which kills
the player and so ends the mission.
Covers: cargo scan, EMP storm, talking heads, directives, goals and objective notices,
waypoints, escort list, wings and waves, wingman messages, fighters attacking the player,
bombers and a kamikaze against a corvette, beams, turrets, a destroyed subsystem, damage
arcs, two capital ships breaking up (one in front of the player, one behind), a
shockwave over the player, asteroids, IFF change, warp in and out, and the supernova.
autotest: player stays still
$End Notes:

$Mission Desc:
 XSTR("Autotest: cargo scan, then a chain of events ending in a supernova.", -1)
$end_multi_text

